# These bytes are the test subject, not just its input.
#
# Requirement 3.1 says a map ADP did not change comes back byte-identical, and the tests check
# that by comparing what the writer produced against the file on disk. With core.autocrlf on,
# git would rewrite the line endings on checkout and the test would be measuring git rather
# than the writer - and `crlf-line-endings.owm` and `lf-line-endings.owm` would become the
# same file, which is the one thing that pair exists to disprove.
#
# `no-trailing-newline.owm` is equally at risk from any tool that helpfully adds one.
*.owm -text
